/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134840652,imgsize-114044.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi's claim that President Murmu accepted 'vote theft' allegation incorrect: Report]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhis-claim-that-president-murmu-accepted-vote-theft-incorrect-report/articleshow/134839913.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134839913.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Regarding the President's response during their interaction, Rahul Gandhi had said, "I sat in quite an unbelievable meeting. First, we took a memorandum to the President of India. In that memorandum, we clearly stated that the Prime Minister, HM Amit Shah, and CEC Gyanesh Kumar had conspired to destroy Indian democracy. The President in no way denied what we said, questioned what we said, or argued what we said."]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhis-claim-that-president-murmu-accepted-vote-theft-incorrect-report/articleshow/134839913.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhis-claim-that-president-murmu-accepted-vote-theft-incorrect-report/articleshow/134839913.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T23:14:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134840061,imgsize-129941.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[JNU sexual harassment claims: BJP questions Rahul Gandhi’s silence]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jnu-sexual-harassment-claims-bjp-questions-rahul-gandhis-silence/articleshow/134837599.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134837599.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[BJP spokesperson Smriti Irani took a strong stance against Rahul Gandhi for failing to address the dismissal of Angomcha Bimol Akoijam from JNU, who faced serious sexual harassment allegations from female students. Irani questioned the sincerity of Gandhi's 'smash the patriarchy' slogan, suggesting that his silence on Akoijam's conduct undermines his political credibility and highlights the need for accountability in political discourse.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jnu-sexual-harassment-claims-bjp-questions-rahul-gandhis-silence/articleshow/134837599.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jnu-sexual-harassment-claims-bjp-questions-rahul-gandhis-silence/articleshow/134837599.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T22:55:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134839318,imgsize-78968.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['City can't be brought to a halt': Delhi Police's rationale for restrictions ahead of CJP stir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/city-cant-be-brought-to-a-halt-delhi-polices-rationale-for-restrictions-ahead-of-cjp-stir/articleshow/134839554.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134839554.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/city-cant-be-brought-to-a-halt-delhi-polices-rationale-for-restrictions-ahead-of-cjp-stir/articleshow/134839554.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/city-cant-be-brought-to-a-halt-delhi-polices-rationale-for-restrictions-ahead-of-cjp-stir/articleshow/134839554.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T22:37:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.